{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018qpjUJuEymvSvSWjFxE9QN","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:36:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"The Linux Foundation — official candidate-facing T&C DOCS, 'Multiple Choice Exams: Important Instructions'\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: []\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-format\", \"exam-pacing\", \"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# Multiple Choice Exams: Important Instructions — Linux Foundation T&C DOCS\n10\t\n11\t> THIS SNAPSHOT OVERTURNS A LOAD-BEARING CHAPTER 1 CLAIM AND A BOOK-LEVEL\n12\t> DO-NOT-RETRIEVE RULE. See the Ch 19 research manifest, \"Notes for the author\",\n13\t> finding 1. This page was NOT among the pages checked by the Ch 1 research.\n14\t\n15\tOfficial Linux Foundation candidate-facing documentation, in the same T&C DOCS\n16\tfamily as the Multiple Choice FAQ. Governs the LF's multiple-choice exams as a\n17\tclass. The KCNA exam page calls KCNA \"an online, proctored, multiple-choice\n18\texam\", placing it in this class.\n19\t\n20\t## Question count — PUBLISHED\n21\t\n22\t\"The multiple-choice exam is delivered online and consists of 60* multiple-choice questions.\"\n23\t\n24\tThe asterisk resolves to a footnote on the same page:\n25\t\n26\t\"* CNPA exam consists of 85 multiple-choice questions.\"\n27\t\n28\tThe asterisk is a CNPA carve-out. It is NOT a \"subject to change\" hedge and NOT\n29\ta statement that the count varies by exam generally.\n30\t\n31\t## Duration — PUBLISHED\n32\t\n33\t\"Candidates have 90* minutes to complete the multiple-choice exam.\"\n34\t\n35\tFootnote: \"* CNPA candidates have 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n36\t\n37\t## Results timing\n38\t\n39\t\"within 24 hours from the time that the exam is completed\"\n40\t\n41\t## Applications and windows during the exam\n42\t\n43\t\"Candidates are not allowed to have other applications or browser windows running except the one on which the Exam is being shown.\"\n44\t\n45\t## Machine constraints\n46\t\n47\t\"You cannot take an exam using a virtual machine.\"\n48\t\n49\t\"One active monitor (either built in or external)\" — \"Dual Monitors are NOT supported\"\n50\t\n51\t\"Latest version of Google Chrome\" recommended. Personal devices preferred over\n52\t\"work-provided devices\".\n53\t\n54\t## Testing location\n55\t\n56\tAcceptable spaces must be \"Clutter-free\" with \"No objects such as paper, writing\n57\timplements, electronic devices\" visible. The space must be \"well lit so that\n58\tproctor is able to see candidate's face, hands, and surrounding work area.\"\n59\tPublic locations — \"coffee shops, stores, open office environments\" — are\n60\tprohibited.\n61\t\n62\t## Identification\n63\t\n64\tValid government-issued photo ID with signature is mandatory. \"The first and last\n65\tname on the ID must exactly match\" the registered information. Acceptable\n66\tdocuments include passports, driver's licenses, and national identity cards.\n67\t\n68\t## Sanctioned countries\n69\t\n70\tTesting is permitted for sanctioned-country citizens only \"OUTSIDE the sanctioned\n71\tcountry\" with matching address documentation.\n72\t\n73\t## Scope caveat — READ BEFORE CITING\n74\t\n75\tThe page is titled for multiple-choice exams generally and DOES NOT NAME KCNA.\n76\tThis is the identical scope situation as the 75% passing score in\n77\tlf-mc-exam-faq-*.md, and the same phrasing discipline applies.\n78\t\n79\t- CORRECT: \"The Linux Foundation publishes a 60-question format for its\n80\t  multiple-choice exams, of which the KCNA is one.\"\n81\t- FALSE, do not write: \"The Linux Foundation does not publish a question count.\"\n82\t- FALSE, do not write: \"The KCNA exam page states the exam has 60 questions.\"\n83\t  (It is in the candidate handbook, not on the exam page. The exam page omits it —\n84\t  that remains confirmed by lf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23.md.)\n85\t\n86\t## Question navigation — NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n87\t\n88\tNo statement about skipping, flagging, marking for review, returning to previous\n89\tquestions, changing an answer, a review screen, or how the exam is submitted.\n90\tConfirmed absent on targeted fetch 2026-08-31.\n91\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2102c50-dbf5-493b-ac44-9adf71c43c9f","uuid":"c7000e61-7587-4e2d-a916-c5cbee22343c","timestamp":"2026-08-31T23:56:09.388Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/lf-mc-exam-important-instructions-2026-08-31.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:36:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"The Linux Foundation — official candidate-facing T&C DOCS, 'Multiple Choice Exams: Important Instructions'\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"kcna-exam-format\", \"exam-pacing\", \"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n---\n\n# Multiple Choice Exams: Important Instructions — Linux Foundation T&C DOCS\n\n> THIS SNAPSHOT OVERTURNS A LOAD-BEARING CHAPTER 1 CLAIM AND A BOOK-LEVEL\n> DO-NOT-RETRIEVE RULE. See the Ch 19 research manifest, \"Notes for the author\",\n> finding 1. This page was NOT among the pages checked by the Ch 1 research.\n\nOfficial Linux Foundation candidate-facing documentation, in the same T&C DOCS\nfamily as the Multiple Choice FAQ. Governs the LF's multiple-choice exams as a\nclass. The KCNA exam page calls KCNA \"an online, proctored, multiple-choice\nexam\", placing it in this class.\n\n## Question count — PUBLISHED\n\n\"The multiple-choice exam is delivered online and consists of 60* multiple-choice questions.\"\n\nThe asterisk resolves to a footnote on the same page:\n\n\"* CNPA exam consists of 85 multiple-choice questions.\"\n\nThe asterisk is a CNPA carve-out. It is NOT a \"subject to change\" hedge and NOT\na statement that the count varies by exam generally.\n\n## Duration — PUBLISHED\n\n\"Candidates have 90* minutes to complete the multiple-choice exam.\"\n\nFootnote: \"* CNPA candidates have 120 minutes to complete the exam.\"\n\n## Results timing\n\n\"within 24 hours from the time that the exam is completed\"\n\n## Applications and windows during the exam\n\n\"Candidates are not allowed to have other applications or browser windows running except the one on which the Exam is being shown.\"\n\n## Machine constraints\n\n\"You cannot take an exam using a virtual machine.\"\n\n\"One active monitor (either built in or external)\" — \"Dual Monitors are NOT supported\"\n\n\"Latest version of Google Chrome\" recommended. Personal devices preferred over\n\"work-provided devices\".\n\n## Testing location\n\nAcceptable spaces must be \"Clutter-free\" with \"No objects such as paper, writing\nimplements, electronic devices\" visible. The space must be \"well lit so that\nproctor is able to see candidate's face, hands, and surrounding work area.\"\nPublic locations — \"coffee shops, stores, open office environments\" — are\nprohibited.\n\n## Identification\n\nValid government-issued photo ID with signature is mandatory. \"The first and last\nname on the ID must exactly match\" the registered information. Acceptable\ndocuments include passports, driver's licenses, and national identity cards.\n\n## Sanctioned countries\n\nTesting is permitted for sanctioned-country citizens only \"OUTSIDE the sanctioned\ncountry\" with matching address documentation.\n\n## Scope caveat — READ BEFORE CITING\n\nThe page is titled for multiple-choice exams generally and DOES NOT NAME KCNA.\nThis is the identical scope situation as the 75% passing score in\nlf-mc-exam-faq-*.md, and the same phrasing discipline applies.\n\n- CORRECT: \"The Linux Foundation publishes a 60-question format for its\n  multiple-choice exams, of which the KCNA is one.\"\n- FALSE, do not write: \"The Linux Foundation does not publish a question count.\"\n- FALSE, do not write: \"The KCNA exam page states the exam has 60 questions.\"\n  (It is in the candidate handbook, not on the exam page. The exam page omits it —\n  that remains confirmed by lf-kcna-exam-page-2026-08-23.md.)\n\n## Question navigation — NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n\nNo statement about skipping, flagging, marking for review, returning to previous\nquestions, changing an answer, a review screen, or how the exam is submitted.\nConfirmed absent on targeted fetch 2026-08-31.\n","numLines":91,"startLine":1,"totalLines":91}}}
