{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GX5suEFoZqNXcnoqgz9zUy","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc\"\n3\tfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:40:00-0400\"\n4\tauthority: \"Correction record. Primary evidence is the Linux Foundation T&C DOCS page cited above.\"\n5\tobjectives_covered: []\n6\tconcepts_covered: [\"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n7\t---\n8\t\n9\t# CORRECTION — the 60-question figure IS published\n10\t\n11\t> SUPERSEDES provenance-kcna-60-questions-2026-08-23.md. That file states\n12\t> \"60 questions — NOT FOUND in any authoritative source.\" THAT STATEMENT IS\n13\t> FALSE and must not be relied on by any drafting or revision stage.\n14\t\n15\t## What the 08-23 file got right\n16\t\n17\tIt correctly identified that the figure is repeated by third parties, and\n18\tcorrectly documented the CNCF-blog community post as one vector. That analysis\n19\tstands.\n20\t\n21\t## What it got wrong\n22\t\n23\tIt generalised from a bounded search to an unbounded claim. It listed the pages\n24\tchecked:\n25\t\n26\t  \"the LF KCNA exam page; the LF MC exam FAQ; the LF general certification FAQ;\n27\t   the LF exam-results handbook page; the CNCF KCNA page; the LFS250 outline\"\n28\t\n29\tThe Linux Foundation T&C DOCS page \"Multiple Choice Exams: Important\n30\tInstructions\" was NOT among them. That page publishes the figure:\n31\t\n32\t\"The multiple-choice exam is delivered online and consists of 60* multiple-choice questions.\"\n33\t\n34\twith the footnote \"* CNPA exam consists of 85 multiple-choice questions.\"\n35\t\n36\t## Current, accurate status of both figures\n37\t\n38\t| Figure | Status | Where published |\n39\t|---|---|---|\n40\t| 90 minutes | PUBLISHED | LF KCNA exam page; MC FAQ; MC Important Instructions |\n41\t| 75% to pass | PUBLISHED | MC FAQ (for MC exams as a class) |\n42\t| 60 questions | PUBLISHED | MC Important Instructions (for MC exams as a class) |\n43\t\n44\tBoth the 75% and the 60 are published for MULTIPLE-CHOICE EXAMS AS A CLASS, in\n45\tthe candidate handbook, and neither appears on the KCNA product page. KCNA is\n46\tplaced in that class by its own exam page (\"an online, proctored, multiple-choice\n47\texam\") and by the MC FAQ's CARE section, which names KCNA explicitly.\n48\t\n49\t## The distinction that survives\n50\t\n51\tThe \"published vs commonly reported\" lesson is NOT dead — it changes shape. The\n52\thonest version is about WHERE an authority publishes a fact, not whether it does:\n53\t\n54\t- The figures are real and published, in the candidate handbook.\n55\t- The product page a candidate is most likely to read omits them.\n56\t- Third parties repeat them without ever citing the handbook, which is why the\n57\t  claim LOOKS unsourced and why its provenance is worth teaching.\n58\t\n59\t## Phrasings\n60\t\n61\t- CORRECT: \"The Linux Foundation publishes both figures in its candidate\n62\t  handbook, for multiple-choice exams as a class; neither appears on the KCNA\n63\t  exam page itself.\"\n64\t- FALSE, do not write: \"The question count travels on repetition alone.\"\n65\t- FALSE, do not write: \"The question count is not anywhere the certifying body writes.\"\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2102c50-dbf5-493b-ac44-9adf71c43c9f","uuid":"90488e8d-2d85-4b6b-8860-c9b3ab85266e","timestamp":"2026-08-31T23:56:09.480Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:/dev/lodestar/Book-KCNA/sources/provenance-kcna-60-questions-2026-08-31.md","content":"---\nsource_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/important-instructions-mc\"\nfetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:40:00-0400\"\nauthority: \"Correction record. Primary evidence is the Linux Foundation T&C DOCS page cited above.\"\nobjectives_covered: []\nconcepts_covered: [\"published-vs-commonly-reported\"]\n---\n\n# CORRECTION — the 60-question figure IS published\n\n> SUPERSEDES provenance-kcna-60-questions-2026-08-23.md. That file states\n> \"60 questions — NOT FOUND in any authoritative source.\" THAT STATEMENT IS\n> FALSE and must not be relied on by any drafting or revision stage.\n\n## What the 08-23 file got right\n\nIt correctly identified that the figure is repeated by third parties, and\ncorrectly documented the CNCF-blog community post as one vector. That analysis\nstands.\n\n## What it got wrong\n\nIt generalised from a bounded search to an unbounded claim. It listed the pages\nchecked:\n\n  \"the LF KCNA exam page; the LF MC exam FAQ; the LF general certification FAQ;\n   the LF exam-results handbook page; the CNCF KCNA page; the LFS250 outline\"\n\nThe Linux Foundation T&C DOCS page \"Multiple Choice Exams: Important\nInstructions\" was NOT among them. That page publishes the figure:\n\n\"The multiple-choice exam is delivered online and consists of 60* multiple-choice questions.\"\n\nwith the footnote \"* CNPA exam consists of 85 multiple-choice questions.\"\n\n## Current, accurate status of both figures\n\n| Figure | Status | Where published |\n|---|---|---|\n| 90 minutes | PUBLISHED | LF KCNA exam page; MC FAQ; MC Important Instructions |\n| 75% to pass | PUBLISHED | MC FAQ (for MC exams as a class) |\n| 60 questions | PUBLISHED | MC Important Instructions (for MC exams as a class) |\n\nBoth the 75% and the 60 are published for MULTIPLE-CHOICE EXAMS AS A CLASS, in\nthe candidate handbook, and neither appears on the KCNA product page. KCNA is\nplaced in that class by its own exam page (\"an online, proctored, multiple-choice\nexam\") and by the MC FAQ's CARE section, which names KCNA explicitly.\n\n## The distinction that survives\n\nThe \"published vs commonly reported\" lesson is NOT dead — it changes shape. The\nhonest version is about WHERE an authority publishes a fact, not whether it does:\n\n- The figures are real and published, in the candidate handbook.\n- The product page a candidate is most likely to read omits them.\n- Third parties repeat them without ever citing the handbook, which is why the\n  claim LOOKS unsourced and why its provenance is worth teaching.\n\n## Phrasings\n\n- CORRECT: \"The Linux Foundation publishes both figures in its candidate\n  handbook, for multiple-choice exams as a class; neither appears on the KCNA\n  exam page itself.\"\n- FALSE, do not write: \"The question count travels on repetition alone.\"\n- FALSE, do not write: \"The question count is not anywhere the certifying body writes.\"\n","numLines":66,"startLine":1,"totalLines":66}}}
