S: Please review the System Requirements, published by PSI, in particular the supported Operating System Information.\"\n190:- \"All browsers are supported, however PSI highly recommends using the latest version of Google Chrome for the best exam scheduling experience, and because the secure browser is Chrome-based and will give a more accurate experience.\"\n191-- \"One active monitor (either built in or external) (NOTE: Dual Monitors are NOT supported)\"\n192-- \"Reliable internet access\"\n193-  - \"Ensure others on the same internet connection are not performing activities that use excessive bandwidth (i.e. holding conference calls, streaming content, gaming, etc.)\"\n--\n231-Confirmed absent on full re-fetch 2026-08-31. The count IS published, on\n232-important-instructions-mc. Absence here is a property of this page only.\n233-\n234:## Question navigation — NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n235-\n236:No statement about skipping, flagging, or reviewing questions.\n237-```\n238-\n239-### A3 · `lf-certification-resources-allowed-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n--\n307----\n308-source_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-rules-and-policies\"\n309-fetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:37:00-0400\"\n310:authority: \"The Linux Foundation — 'Exam Rules and Policies', Candidate Handbook (PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform)\"\n311-objectives_covered: []\n312-concepts_covered: [\"exam-pacing\", \"the-lodestar\"]\n313----\n314-\n315:# Exam Rules and Policies — Linux Foundation Candidate Handbook (PSI BRIDGE)\n316-\n317-## Conduct during the exam — verbatim\n318-\n--\n348-\n349-No statement about whether breaks are permitted during a multiple-choice exam.\n350-\n351:## Question navigation — NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n352-\n353:No statement about skipping, flagging, or reviewing questions.\n354-```\n355-\n356-### A5 · `lf-handbook2-candidate-requirements-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n--\n358----\n359-source_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements\"\n360-fetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:37:00-0400\"\n361:authority: \"The Linux Foundation — 'Candidate Requirements', Candidate Handbook (PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform)\"\n362-objectives_covered: []\n363-concepts_covered: [\"exam-pacing\"]\n364----\n365-\n366:# Candidate Requirements — Linux Foundation Candidate Handbook (PSI BRIDGE)\n367-\n368-Supports Ch 19 §6 (\"The Week Before\") — these are the checks that belong on a\n369-final-week list rather than on exam morning.\n370-\n371-## System and hardware — verbatim\n372-\n373:- \"Supported OS: Please review the System Requirements, published by PSI, in particular the supported Operating System Information.\"\n374-- \"One active monitor (either built in or external) (NOTE: Dual Monitors are NOT supported)\"\n375-- \"The Linux Foundation recommends a screen size of 15\\\" or higher to support the ExamUI.\"\n376-- \"The Linux Foundation recommends a screen resolution of 1080p.\"\n--\n405----\n406-source_url: \"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam\"\n407-fetched_at: \"2026-08-31T18:38:00-0400\"\n408:authority: \"The Linux Foundation — 'Taking the Exam', Candidate Handbook (PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform)\"\n409-objectives_covered: []\n410-concepts_covered: [\"exam-pacing\"]\n411----\n412-\n413:# Taking the Exam — Linux Foundation Candidate Handbook (PSI BRIDGE)\n414-\n415-## Check-in window — verbatim\n416-\n--\n438-The page does not state whether check-in time counts against the 90 minutes.\n439-DO NOT ASSERT EITHER WAY. See the Ch 19 manifest, Gaps.\n440-\n441:## Question navigation — NOT PRESENT ON PAGE\n442-\n443:No statement about the exam interface, flagging, or reviewing answers.\n444-```\n445-\n446-### A7 · `provenance-kcna-60-questions-2026-08-31.md` (new)\n--\n561-\n562-## Gaps\n563-\n564:Flagged for the drafting stage. **Do not invent facts to fill these.**\n565-\n566:### G1 — Question navigation, flagging, and skipping is UNPUBLISHED · blocks part of §3\n567-\n568:This is the most consequential gap. The §4 section plan for §3 specifies \"the first pass, **flagging and skipping**, the second pass\" as the chapter's pacing method, and places a ★ Fixed Point on it. **No Linux Foundation or PSI page I could reach states that the multiple-choice exam interface supports flagging a question, skipping a question, returning to a previous question, or reviewing answers before submission.**\n569-\n570-Confirmed absent on targeted fetch across six official pages: `faq-mc`, `important-instructions-mc`, `lf-handbook2`, `lf-handbook2/exam-rules-and-policies`, `lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements`, `lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam`.\n571-\n572-The negative result is well-established, not a thin search. Two viable responses, author's call:\n573-\n574:- **(a)** Write the pacing rule in terms the interface cannot invalidate — budget the clock, do not spend disproportionate time on any single item, answer everything since there is no penalty for a wrong answer — and drop the specific flag/skip mechanic.\n575:- **(b)** Keep flag-and-skip but frame it conditionally (\"if the interface offers a way to mark a question and return to it, use it\"), which is honest but weak for a ★ Fixed Point.\n576-\n577-I'd recommend **(a)**. A Fixed Point should not rest on an unverified interface affordance, and A4's sourced \"no writing outside the Exam console screen\" already gives §3 a stronger, fully-sourced spine.\n578-\n--\n636-\n637-[Omitted long context line]\n638-\n639:This is a Chapter 1 revision decision, outside Ch 19's scope. Flagging it here because Ch 19 §3 cannot be drafted coherently until it is settled — §3 either inherits Ch 1's claim and repeats an error, or contradicts a shipped chapter.\n640-\n641-### 2. §3's design survives the correction, and improves\n642-"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2102c50-dbf5-493b-ac44-9adf71c43c9f","uuid":"601d2ef2-f3d3-41e5-9201-dd0b695a6012","timestamp":"2026-08-31T23:56:23.871