DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/tips-cka-and-ckad\"}]\n\nI found the search results for Linux Foundation certification ExamUI multiple choice exam interface information. The search returned official Linux Foundation documentation resources related to their candidate handbook and exam interface.\n\nThe Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook covers the ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams section, which is part of the comprehensive guide for candidates using the PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform.\n\nThe primary resource for this information is the official Linux Foundation documentation (T&C DOCS) that provides candidate-facing resources including details about the Exam User Interface: Configuration & Features and specific ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams guidance.\n\nYou can access the specific documentation page on ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams at: https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-user-interface/examui-multiple-choice-exams\n\nThis documentation is part of the handbook that applies to Linux Foundation Exams proctored using the PSI BRIDGE Proctoring Service.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2102c50-dbf5-493b-ac44-9adf71c43c9f","uuid":"5cec5717-4a49-471c-8f32-501e87877e89","timestamp":"2026-08-31T23:56:35.790Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Linux Foundation certification ExamUI multiple choice exam interface candidate handbook","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01CCSoyi2oxvgZ4qTRC8BbG3","content":[{"title":"ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-user-interface/examui-multiple-choice-exams"},{"title":"Exam User Interface: Configuration & Features | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-user-interface"},{"title":"ExamUI: Performance Based Exams | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-user-interface/examui-performance-based-exams"},{"title":"Candidate Requirements | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements"},{"title":"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform) | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2"},{"title":"Exam UI: SkillCred Exam | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook1/exam-ui-skillcred-exam"},{"title":"Linuxfoundation","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-candidate-handbook*"},{"title":"Linux Foundation Credential Exam: Candidate Handbook | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook1"},{"title":"Certification | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification"},{"title":"Important Instructions: CKA and CKAD | T&C DOCS (Candidate Facing Resources)","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/tips-cka-and-ckad"}]},"I found the search results for Linux Foundation certification ExamUI multiple choice exam interface information. The search returned official Linux Foundation documentation resources related to their candidate handbook and exam interface.\n\nThe Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook covers the ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams section, which is part of the comprehensive guide for candidates using the PSI BRIDGE Proctoring platform.\n\nThe primary resource for this information is the official Linux Foundation documentation (T&C DOCS) that provides candidate-facing resources including details about the Exam User Interface: Configuration & Features and specific ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams guidance.\n\nYou can access the specific documentation page on ExamUI: Multiple Choice Exams at: https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/exam-user-interface/examui-multiple-choice-exams\n\nThis documentation is part of the handbook that applies to Linux Foundation Exams proctored using the PSI BRIDGE Proctoring Service."],"durationSeconds":5.422349900000001,"searchCount":1}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GFqBkDgGKqFmjHbhF7KvWd","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"PSI Bridge proctoring platform candidate exam interface flag question review navigation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using ...\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2\"},{\"title\":\"Live Remote Proctoring\",\"url\":\"https://www.nchec.org/live-remote-proctoring\"},{\"title\":\"Candidate Requirements\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements\"},{\"title\":\"Taking the Exam\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam\"},{\"title\":\"PSI Remote Testing Tutorial (Test the Secure Browser) + ADD ...\",\"url\":\"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/psi-remote-testing-tutorial-test-the-secure-browser-+-add-appointment-to-your-online-calendar\"},{\"title\":\"Psionline\",\"url\":\"https://info.psionline.com/PSIBridge-Overview/\"},{\"title\":\"PSI Bridge Reviews in 2026\",\"url\":\"https://sourceforge.net/software/product/PSI-Bridge/\"},{\"title\":\"LF Migration to PSI Bridge Proctoring Platform 2021-2022 - Linux ...\",\"url\":\"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/bridge-migration-2021/\"},{\"title\":\"PSI Bridge allows you to take your proctored exam anytime, anywhere.\",\"url\":\"https://content.psionline.com/hubfs/PSI_Bridge_Full_Guide_AWS-7-21-20.pdf?hsLang=en\"},{\"title\":\"GPS, PSI Bridge Secure Browser and Google Chrome Installation ...\",\"url\":\"https://hiset.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/hiset_gps-google-chrome-and-exam-browser-installation.pdf\"}]\n\nI've performed the web search for \"PSI Bridge proctoring platform candidate exam interface.\" Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview of PSI Bridge\n\nPSI Bridge is PSI's remote assessment platform that gives candidates 24/7 access, allowing them to test from home with an internet-enabled location, where they must provide a computer with Google Chrome, a camera, microphone, and an internet connection. It is an easy-to-use platform and allows the same standard security procedures as implemented in PSI's global test center network.\n\n## Exam Interface Features\n\nThe online proctored exam is taken on PSI's Proctoring Platform \"Bridge\", using the PSI Secure Browser (a web browser created to guarantee a secure exam delivery over a virtual connection).\n\nThere are changes and improvements to the ExamUI (the environment provisioned for your assessment). Some key features include:\n\n- A timer that displays the actual time remaining (in minutes) and provides an alert with 30, 15, or 5 minute remaining\n- The content panel remains the same (presented on the Left Hand Side of the ExamUI)\n\n## Dashboard and Results\n\nThe Proctored Exam Results Dashboard allows you to see proctored exam results in your LMS and view specific students' exams alongside flagged violations and ability to see the annotated video.\n\nThe search results provide general information about the PSI Bridge platform, though they don't specifically detail navigation features like \"flag question\" or \"review navigation\" functions that you mentioned in your query.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d2102c50-dbf5-493b-ac44-9adf71c43c9f","uuid":"70ea19b6-4cb4-4856-8f83-d2f53c55bc93","timestamp":"2026-08-31T23:56:37.678Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"PSI Bridge proctoring platform candidate exam interface flag question review navigation","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Nkd2rvzaebxkMetgwekeGX","content":[{"title":"Linux Foundation Certification Exam: Candidate Handbook (using ...","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2"},{"title":"Live Remote Proctoring","url":"https://www.nchec.org/live-remote-proctoring"},{"title":"Candidate Requirements","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/candidate-requirements"},{"title":"Taking the Exam","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/taking-the-exam"},{"title":"PSI Remote Testing Tutorial (Test the Secure Browser) + ADD ...","url":"https://docs.linuxfoundation.org/tc-docs/certification/lf-handbook2/psi-remote-testing-tutorial-test-the-secure-browser-+-add-appointment-to-your-online-calendar"},{"title":"Psionline","url":"https://info.psionline.com/PSIBridge-Overview/"},{"title":"PSI Bridge Reviews in 2026","url":"https://sourceforge.net/software/product/PSI-Bridge/"},{"title":"LF Migration to PSI Bridge Proctoring Platform 2021-2022 - Linux ...","url":"https://training.linuxfoundation.org/bridge-migration-2021/"},{"title":"PSI Bridge allows you to take your proctored exam anytime, anywhere.","url":"https://content.psionline.com/hubfs/PSI_Bridge_Full_Guide_AWS-7-21-20.pdf?hsLang=en"},{"title":"GPS, PSI Bridge Secure Browser and Google Chrome Installation ...","url":"https://hiset.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/hiset_gps-google-chrome-and-exam-browser-installation.pdf"}]},"I've performed the web search for \"PSI Bridge proctoring platform candidate exam interface.\" Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview of PSI Bridge\n\nPSI Bridge is PSI's remote assessment platform that gives candidates 24/7 access, allowing them to test from home with an internet-enabled location, where they must provide a computer with Google Chrome, a camera, microphone, and an internet connection. It is an easy-to-use platform and allows the same standard security procedures as implemented in PSI's global test center network.\n\n## Exam Interface Features\n\nThe online proctored exam is taken on PSI's Proctoring Platform \"Bridge\", using the PSI Secure Browser (a web browser created to guarantee a secure exam delivery over a virtual connection).\n\nThere are changes and improvements to the ExamUI (the environment provisioned for your assessment). Some key features include:\n\n- A timer that displays the actual time remaining (in minutes) and provides an alert with 30, 15, or 5 minute remaining\n- The content panel remains the same (presented on the Left Hand Side of the ExamUI)\n\n## Dashboard and Results\n\nThe Proctored Exam Results Dashboard allows you to see proctored exam results in your LMS and view specific students' exams alongside flagged violations and ability to see the annotated video.\n\nThe search results provide general information about the PSI Bridge platform, though they don't specifically detail navigation features like \"flag question\" or \"review navigation\" functions that you mentioned in your query."],"durationSeconds":8.02655410000001,"searchCount":1}}
